<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudolf Stüssi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1443">1443</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Rudolf Stussi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudolf Stüssi was burgomaster of Zürich who led the city into alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war">Old Zürich War</a>. He was killed on 22 July 1443 at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-st-jakob-an-der-sihl">Battle of St. Jakob an der Sihl</a> while defending the bridge over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sihl">Sihl</a> outside the city. His policy of alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> against the other confederates ended in Zürich's defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-stussi.jpg" alt="Rudolf Stüssi" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Werner Schodoler; upload by sidonius 09:58, 24 July 2007 (UTC) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zuerichkrieg_1444.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Stüssi's father came from Glarus, became a citizen of Zürich in 1375 and held city offices from 1388. Rudolf himself was elected to city offices from 1414, served as Zürich's envoy in the Old Swiss Confederacy in 1424 and became mayor in 1430, holding the post until his death. In 1433 he went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> as Zürich's representative at the coronation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-holy-roman-emperor">Sigismund of Luxembourg</a> and was knighted there. He lived in a house later called the Stüssihofstatt, about 100 m north-east of the Rathaus.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p>As mayor Stüssi sought to extend the rule and influence of his city, and his ambitions are held to have caused the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war">Old Zürich War</a>, which broke out in 1440. When Count Friedrich VII of Toggenburg died in 1436 without an heir or a will, Zürich under Stüssi claimed the Toggenburg lands, while the cantons of Schwyz and Glarus made counter-claims with the backing of the other cantons. In 1442 Stüssi allied Zürich with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Frederick III, Holy Roman Emperor</a>, against the Confederacy.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-st-jakob-an-der-sihl">Battle of St. Jakob an der Sihl</a> he held the bridge over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sihl">Sihl</a> to cover the retreat of Zürich's army. According to chroniclers he was killed by a confederate soldier hiding beneath the bridge. Another version of the story has him stopping in the middle of the bridge, brandishing his broad battle-axe and shouting &quot;Halt, citizens, halt!&quot; A man of Zürich is said to have answered, &quot;May God's lightning blast thee! All this evil comes from thee alone,&quot; and run him through with his lance. Either way, he fell defending his own city's retreat.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Rudolf Stüssi” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The confederates defeated the Zürich army at the Battle of St. Jakob an der Sihl in 1443, where the burgomaster <b>Rudolf Stüssi</b> was killed, and besieged the city; in the peace settlement of 1450 Zürich had to abandon the Habsburg alliance.</blockquote><a href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Canton of Zürich · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>At the gates of Zürich, the confederate army led by Schwyz defeated the Zürich forces and their Austrian allies; the burgomaster <b>Rudolf Stüssi</b> was killed defending the Sihl bridge.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-22">22 July in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Zurich, in what is now <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. Died in Zurich, in what is now <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=47.37,8.54&amp;year=1433" aria-label="Zurich on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of Rudolf Stüssi"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n60.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5493 6039h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5493 6039h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=47.37,8.54&amp;year=1433">What was here in 1433? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
